winebus: nothing asked of the vibration, nothing rewritten.

mgvf-0009 stores "no options" as all zeros and says that testing for that is
the write path's job. One of the two write paths did it and the other did not:
a report that went out through the USB emulation reached the rewrite with mode
0 and gain 0 -- and a gain of 0 is not an absence there, it is a REQUEST, for
silence. So on that route every motor value a client asked for was quietly
zeroed, and the pad never buzzed however hard the game asked for it.

Measured on 2026-09-09 with an XInput write and no option set anywhere:
  dualsense_vibration_fixup ... motors 0/255 -> 0/0

The test moves into the one function both paths call.

Signed-off-by: MacGameVideoFix
---
--- a/dlls/winebus.sys/main.c
